        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0408" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg274"/>

                <head>No. 188.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21, 1888</date>.
                        (Received May 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 600.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a letter sent by me to the managers of Pootung Wharf and Godown Company. I
                    send it to you as explanatory of my action touching the important question of
                    the bonding of kerosene in China, so far as it has been presented to this
                    legation.</p>
                <p>The question is still unsettled.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d188-a1.xml" xpointer="d188-a1"/>
            </div>
